  "question": {
    "text": "The ratio of spin-only magnetic moment values &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cr</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cr</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is _______",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In case of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;ion , the valence shell electronic configuration is same whether the ligand is strong field or weak field.</p><p>The spin only magnetic moment ,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mi>BM</mi></math></p><p>The valence shell electronic configuration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, hence, it has three unpaired electrons.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mtext>eff&#160;</mtext></msub></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cr</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>15</mn></msqrt><mtext>&#160;B.M.&#160;</mtext></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mtext>eff&#160;</mtext></msub></math>of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cr</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>15</mn></msqrt><mtext>&#160;B.M.&#160;</mtext></math></p><p>Ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
